&gt;&gt; Abstract:<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 This document describes Merkle Tree certificates, a n=
ew certificate<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 type for use with TLS.=C2=A0 A relying party that reg=
ularly fetches<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 information from a transparency service can use this =
certificate type<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 as a size optimization over more conventional mechani=
sms with post-<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 quantum signatures.=C2=A0 Merkle Tree certificates in=
tegrate the roles of<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 X.509 and Certificate Transparency, achieving compara=
ble security<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 properties with a smaller message size, at the cost o=
f more limited<br>
&gt;&gt;=C2=A0 =C2=A0 applicability.<br>
